  "understanding": "The supplied source distinguishes transport submission, response decoding, future delivery, and protocol acceptance. Network heartbeats use a request-shape predicate and an optional callback; other requests enter the consumer channel. Network pipeline submission sends before handing a future to a separate decoder. Neither transport success nor future delivery alone establishes replication progress, current authority, or durable acceptance. The in-memory variant ignores heartbeat-handler registration, but its RPC and pipeline implementations remain unread.",
